# Schema selectors and configuration forms

A selector describes the value a form accepts and how the native interface helps someone supply it. It is not a permission grant or a promise that a target is currently available. Preserve the schema, value type, filters and validation supplied by Home Assistant.

<h2 id="selection">Registry, provider and destination selection</h2>

Entity, device, area, floor, label and target selectors use stable identities and native filters; follow [target pickers](target-pickers.html#ha-ctrl-008-capabilities). Config-entry, app, backup-location, serial-port and provider selectors refer to different resources: do not flatten them into a list of entity IDs. Attribute selection depends on its parent entity. Statistic selection refers to a statistic identity that may not have a current state entity.

Assist pipeline, conversation agent, speech-to-text, text-to-speech and voice choices must retain provider relationships and permission boundaries. A native selection can use a cloud provider; label a verified external processing boundary where the actual integration establishes one. Language, country and timezone are separate preferences. A language choice must not silently change units or the household timezone.

