<h2 id="values">Scalar values, choices and presentation variants</h2>

Number selectors retain min/max/step and native slider or box mode. Boolean retains a boolean, not the strings “yes” and “no”. Date, datetime, time, duration and period have different serialisation; a duration is not a clock time. RGB colour is a channel value, while colour temperature has its own units and device limits. Do not convert one into the other just to reuse a widget.

Select preserves single versus multiple selection, labelled options and the declared custom-value policy. Choose exposes the selected branch and its dependent fields; keep a stored inactive branch only if the native schema does so. Constant and button-toggle values still need their real purpose. A placeholder is not a label or default answer. Entity-name and UI state-content selectors configure presentation, not entity identity.

Device class, state class and unit-of-measurement choices constrain interpretation of data. Explain their relationship and preserve contextual filters. Changing a displayed unit string does not convert recorded values. Use [numbers and data](../content/numbers-and-data.html) and [locale, units and time](locale-units-and-time.html).

