<h2 id="structured">Actions, conditions, triggers and structured input</h2>

Action, condition and trigger selectors retain native typed editors; these are not ordinary free text. A trigger starts evaluation, conditions determine whether actions run, and actions request work. A selector-of-selectors chooses a schema, not its eventual value. Automation-behaviour and numeric-threshold selectors are internal typed configuration with their own constraints. Keep advanced options discoverable without forcing every person into code.

Object and template editors need a visible label, expected shape, syntax feedback and retained input after rejection. A valid template can still produce a value the consumer cannot use. Separate syntax validation, schema validation and execution; checking a draft must not execute it. File input must state permitted content and actual upload destination before upload. QR code is an output representation or specific selector contract, not a substitute for a readable equivalent; do not expose secrets in a fallback.

